    "result_text": "No stale references. The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released **version 2 of the owner identity**. All changes are consistent with the spec and the build/tests pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`).\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in \u2014 every identifier changes, none reproduces a V1 value):**\n- Added `OwnerIdentityVersion` (new file) as the single source of the fixed `\"V2\"` tag, plus `regionCode(plain)` which appends the tag to the region used *inside* identifiers (e.g. `NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`).\n- `buildMemberId` now composes the member id from the V2 region code, so the member id becomes e.g. `NSWV2261A2B3C4D\u2026`.\n- `HouseholdNormalizer.key` now prefixes the hashed key with `V2|`, so the `householdId` changes.\n- `buildIdentityKey` now hashes `V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`, so the `identityKey` changes.\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain (V2 tag only inside identifiers):**\n- `locality` and `timezone` (in `OwnerMapper`) and the region in `OwnerSegment` now derive from `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeAndCity(postcode, city)` \u2014 plain `NSW`, never the tagged form. Removed the now-obsolete `OwnerLocality.forMemberId` (it would have leaked the V2 tag into locality).\n\n**Response shape:**\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema in `openapi.yml`; `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` moved off the top level into a nested `identity` object; added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`. `OwnerMapper` builds the nested identity object and sets `apiVersion = 2`.\n\n**Audit event \u2192 schema version 2:**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained a `schemaVersion` field (`AUDIT_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`); its `memberId` is the recomputed V2 member id. The verified audit line reads `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV2...\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\n**Request fields:** unchanged.\n\nDescriptions in `openapi.yml` and the relevant Javadoc were updated to match the new behaviour.",
