    "probe_text": "Based on the code, here's every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in the exact order they execute. The endpoint is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, taking an `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n\n## Validations (in order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the method. Enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`. Failure \u2192 **403**.\n\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** \u2014 the endpoint parameter is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (interface is `@Validated`). Field constraints fire here:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title`: `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)`\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - Failure \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, the stored owner is returned as **200 OK** and *nothing below runs* (no create).\n\nThen, inside `buildOwnerToCreate`:\n\n4. **`resolveAddressFields`** \u2014 canonicalizes/normalizes address fields (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`).\n\n5. **`validateRequiredFields`** \u2014 re-checks firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone present. Failure \u2192 **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n6. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 4-digit format **and** postcode-matches-city region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Failure \u2192 **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException`).\n\n7. **`ownerMapper.toOwner`** \u2014 MapStruct maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (ignores id/pets).\n\n8. **`TelephoneNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 converts to E.164 (strips separators, defaults `+61`, drops leading 0), requires `+` then 8\u201315 digits and enforces national lengths (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Failure \u2192 **400** (`InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])`).\n\n9. **`normalizeEmail`** \u2014 lower-cases, validates syntax, and rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Failure \u2192 **400**.\n\n10. **`validateRegistrationDate`** \u2014 must not be a future date. Failure \u2192 **400**.\n\n11. **Default + business-day roll** \u2014 if registrationDate is null, set to today; then `toBusinessDay` rolls the date forward off weekends and the 2026 public-holiday set.\n\n12. **`resolveHouseholdIdentity`** \u2014 computes `householdId` (SHA-256 of `TAG|normalizedLastName|postcode`) and `identityKey` (SHA-256 of `V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`). Then:\n    - If **not** `sharesHousehold`: `rejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`) on identity-key collision with a non-deleted owner.\n    - If `sharesHousehold`: instead flags `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (same last-name Soundex + postcode).\n\n13. **`enforceCreateLimits`** \u2014 city owner count \u2265 50 \u2192 **409** (`OwnerCityFullException`); same-day owner count \u2265 100 \u2192 **429** (`OwnerDailyLimitException`). Returns the pre-save day count (used for the bulk-signup warning threshold of 80).\n\nNote: the `Owner` entity's own constraints (`@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone/firstName/lastName, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone) are **not** actively invoked on this path \u2014 there's no `@Valid` on the entity and no explicit validator call; validation happens on the DTO.\n\n## Side-effects (in order)\n\n14. **`finalizeOwnerForCreate`** \u2014 mutates the owner: sets a de-duplicated `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` with Luhn check digit), `namesakeCount`, `householdSize` (existing household members + 1), and `membershipLevelCap`.\n\n15. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`em.persist` for new id), within `@Transactional`. No JPA lifecycle callbacks/entity listeners exist.\n\nThen, in `createdOwnerResponse`:\n\n16. **Audit log line** \u2014 SLF4J logger `\"AUDIT\"`: `owner created id=\u2026 memberId=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`.\n\n17. **Structured audit event** \u2014 `\"AUDIT\"` logger, JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent{seq, schemaVersion=2, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, event=\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, using a process-wide `AtomicLong` sequence (Jackson-serialized).\n\n18. **Welcome notification** \u2014 SLF4J logger `\"NOTIFY\"`: `welcome notification enqueued for owner id=\u2026 memberId=\u2026`. (Log-only; no real email/queue.)\n\n19. **Response DTO mutation** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` (day count > 80), `capacityWarning`, and `riskFlag` on the returned `OwnerDto`.\n\n20. **Location header** \u2014 adds `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n21. **Idempotency store write** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was present, caches the response body under that key so a replay returns 200 instead of re-creating.\n\n22. Returns **201 Created**.\n\nA few things worth flagging: the \"audit event\" and \"welcome notification\" are just log emissions on dedicated loggers \u2014 no Spring `ApplicationEvent`, message broker, or actual email is involved. The `saveOwner` call is the only transactional boundary; the controller method itself is not `@Transactional`, so the many read counts (city/day/namesake/duplicate scans via `findAllOwners`) run outside a shared transaction with the save."
  },
